Subject: [PATCH 6.6.y 0/5] can: bcm: backport of 5 patches that failed to
 apply to 6.6-stable

This resubmits "can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer
values" (commit 749179c2e25b95d22499ed29096b3e02d6dfd2b4 upstream),
which failed to apply to the 6.6-stable tree, together with 4 further
bcm.c patches from the same upstream series that depend on it and
would otherwise fail for the same reason.

Patch 1/5 differs from the upstream commit: upstream additionally
moves the pre-existing traffic_flags/RX_LOCAL/RX_OWN computation in
bcm_rx_handler() under the new bcm_rx_update_lock. That code was
introduced by commit fec846fa7eddf7bb651bf88bd78c7db1410ae3b1 ("can:
bcm: add recvmsg flags for own, local and remote traffic"), which is
not present on 6.6-stable and not itself a stable candidate (pure
feature addition, no Cc: stable). That hunk is omitted; the actual
KCSAN-reported race (bcm_rx_setup() timer/filter updates and the
RTR-frame snapshot in bcm_rx_handler()) is unaffected and fully
addressed by the remaining locking. See the patch changelog for
details.

Patches 2-5 are unmodified backports that apply cleanly once 1/5 is
in place; they were previously reported as FAILED for the same
underlying reason (missing bcm_rx_update_lock prerequisite), not for
independent conflicts.

This assumes the 3 already-queued bcm.c patches for 6.6-stable
("can: bcm: defer rx_op deallocation to workqueue to fix thrtimer
UAF", "can: bcm: fix lockless bound/ifindex race and silent RX_SETUP
failure", "can: bcm: add missing rcu list annotations and
operations") have landed by the time this is applied. If not, please
let me know and I will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (5):
  can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer values
  can: bcm: extend bcm_tx_lock usage for data and timer updates
  can: bcm: validate frame length in bcm_rx_setup() for RTR replies
  can: bcm: add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal
  can: bcm: fix stale rx/tx ops after device removal

